10. Research Architecture

10.1 The Complete System

The complete human–algorithm dynamical system can be represented as:

\boxed{ \text{Platform} \leftrightarrow \text{Human} \leftrightarrow \text{Behavior} \leftrightarrow \text{Outcome} } 

with feedback:

Y(t) \rightarrow \text{Personal Testimony} \rightarrow \text{Social Reinforcement} \rightarrow X(t+1) 

The research proceeds through six stages:

Stage Variable Measurement
I. Epistemic Environment $E, A, S, M, P$ Content analysis; platform audits
II. Exposure $X(t)$ Panel instrumentation; sock-puppet audits
III. Perception $C(t), T(t)$ Credibility scales; parasocial interaction scales
IV. Belief Updating $B(t+1)$ Bayesian model; pre/post measures
V. Behavioral Conversion $B_h(t)$ Purchase intent; adoption measures
VI. Health Outcome $Y(t)$ Clinical endpoints; anxiety scales

10.2 Layer 1: Literature Analysis

Three lenses are essential:

1. Social Cognitive Theory: Observational learning, self-efficacy, self-regulation.
2. MAIN Model and Heuristic Systematic Model: Expertise heuristic triggers, effort reduction.
3. Infodemic Management: WHO five-phase process (signal detection, verification, risk assessment, response design, outreach).

10.3 Layer 2: Content Analysis

· Validated tools: Patient Education Materials Assessment Tool for Audiovisual Material.
· Commercial traceability: same supplement batch or lot promoted across creators.
· Risk disclosure coding: presence or absence of side effect and interaction warnings.
· Corporate political activity techniques: undermining scientists, promoting personal empowerment, lobbying against regulation.

10.4 Layer 3: Human Decision Experiments

Variable Levels
Follower count 10,000 vs. 500,000
Physical appearance Fit vs. average
Parasocial cue Personal story vs. clinical summary
Scientific vocabulary High vs. low density
Actual citation quality Present vs. absent
Platform TikTok vs. Instagram
Commercial disclosure Present vs. absent

Outcome measures: credibility ratings (multidimensional), persuasion outcomes, belief strength (pre/post), purchase intent, self-diagnosis intention.

10.5 Layer 4: Algorithmic Exposure Modeling

· Sock-puppet audits: Fresh accounts engaging with magnesium content, measuring subsequent recommendations.
· Digital trace donation: Consented panel instrumentation.
· WHO EARS platform methodology: Standardized taxonomy for infodemic listening.

10.6 Layer 5: Risk and Outcome Analysis

Risk endpoints: poly-supplement interaction risk (stack size greater than five compounds); health anxiety; self-tracking anxiety; delayed professional consultation; techno-hypochondria (biometric obsession, digital catastrophizing, algorithmic feedback need); false positive rate of device alerts.

Benefit endpoints: improved health literacy; positive behavior change; evidence amplification versus degradation.

